      "writtenOn": "2023-12-07T22:38:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "aapt2 accepts either a list of flags (i.e. the contents of the merged file), or a file to read the flags from. Thus, we cannot pass the inputs like `--feature-flags @file1.txt @file2.txt`. To pass in all the flags without combining the files, we would have to cat all the file contents and pass them as an argument.\n\nHowever, I could verify with the `aapt2` owner that the `--feature-flags` flag can be passed in multiple times, e.g. `--feature-flags @file1.txt --feature-flags @file2.txt`. With this, I believe that there is no need to generate a combined file and the cat logic can be removed😊",
      "parentUuid": "c01ca216_211f86ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 21
      },
